meta {
  name: Get Lead Sources
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/owner-dashboard/lead-sources?range=lastMonth
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  range: lastMonth
  ~producerIds: 
  ~leadSourceIds: __none__
  ~policyTypes: Auto
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{ownerDashboardToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("sorts by premium, with No source always last", function () {
    const rows = res.getBody().rows;
    const named = rows.filter((row) => row.leadSourceId !== null);
    for (let i = 1; i < named.length; i++) {
      expect(named[i - 1].premium).to.be.at.least(named[i].premium);
    }
    const none = rows.findIndex((row) => row.leadSourceId === null);
    if (none !== -1) {
      expect(none).to.equal(rows.length - 1);
      expect(rows[none].name).to.equal("No source");
    }
  });

  test("a conversion rate is a number or a stated gap — never both, never neither", function () {
    const { rows, totals } = res.getBody();
    for (const row of [...rows, totals]) {
      if (row.convPct === null) {
        expect(["no_quotes", "too_few_quotes"]).to.include(row.convGap);
      } else {
        expect(row.convGap).to.equal(null);
      }
    }
  });

  test("agrees with the summary card under the same filter", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().totals.premium).to.equal(bru.getVar("ownerSummaryPremium"));
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /owner-dashboard/lead-sources — the lead-source matrix (PAC-135)

  Per lead source: **Conv %** · **Vol** · **Premium**, plus a total row, for the
  selected window.

  - **Module / permission / scope / query:** identical to
    `GET /owner-dashboard/summary` — see that request's docs.

  The mockup calls this an "ROI matrix". There is no cost data anywhere in the
  system, so it is a performance table, not a return on anything.

  ## The columns
  | field | meaning |
  |---|---|
  | volume | **leads received** in the window, by their creation day |
  | premium | sold premium, summed from policy lines |
  | quotedPremium | quoted premium, from quote-recap lines |
  | convPct | sold ÷ quoted premium × 100 — the same premium-based rule as the closing-ratio card |
  | convGap | why `convPct` is `null`: `no_quotes`, or `too_few_quotes` (under one recap per ten sales) |

  `volume` answers a different question from the other two — leads *received*
  versus business *written* — so a source can show volume with no premium yet,
  or premium from leads that arrived before the window.

  ## Which source a record belongs to
  **The lead owns the source.** A sale and the quotes behind it resolve it through
  their lead, so correcting a lead moves all of them together and a conversion
  rate always divides like by like. A deal's own `leadSourceId` is the fallback —
  for a deal with no lead, and for a lead that has none of its own.

  Everything left over lands in **No source**, always last. On migrated data that
  row is large: about two thirds of historic deals carry no source and no lead
  link. It is the honest size of the gap, and hiding it would make the table's
  total disagree with the card — `totals.premium` equals the summary's
  `premium.current` under any filter.

  ## How the filters apply
  | filter | sold · quoted | volume |
  |---|---|---|
  | period | sold date · quote date | lead creation day |
  | producerIds | ✓ — "this producer's sources" | ✓ |
  | leadSourceIds | ✓ — narrows the rows | ✓ |
  | policyTypes | ✓ | ✗ **cannot apply** |

  A lead is not a policy, and `policiesOfInterest` is empty on every migrated
  lead, so a line-of-business filter on `volume` would zero the column for all
  of history. Volume means "how many leads this source sent", whatever they went
  on to buy.

  A migrated lead's creation date is date-only, stored as UTC midnight. It is
  read as that calendar day — not as the Chicago evening before it — the same
  provenance rule `quoteDateYmd` applies.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "period": { "key": "lastMonth", "current": { "from": "2026-08-01", "to": "2026-08-31" }, "previous": { "from": "2026-07-01", "to": "2026-07-31" } },
    "rows": [
      { "leadSourceId": "66f0…a1", "name": "Mailer", "volume": 329, "premium": 72882.4, "quotedPremium": 69280, "convPct": 105.2, "convGap": null },
      { "leadSourceId": null, "name": "No source", "volume": 4, "premium": 9120, "quotedPremium": 0, "convPct": null, "convGap": "no_quotes" }
    ],
    "totals": { "volume": 333, "premium": 82002.4, "quotedPremium": 69280, "convPct": 118.4, "convGap": null }
  }
  ```

  ## Errors
  Same as `GET /owner-dashboard/summary`: `400` bad query · `401` · `403`.
}
